WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.819
Daisy Ridley was plucked from obscurity and
cast as scavenger Rey in Star Wars: The Force

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:05.819
Awakens.

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:09.660
Claiming one of the most coveted roles in
Hollywood, she instantly became the face of

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.960
the new Star Wars trilogy.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.430
Her monumental rise has been a real-life fairytale,
but it wasn't just handed to her.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.940
Here's how she landed the role that changed
her life.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.000
"Hey, I'm fun and I'm cool, come along on
this ride with me."

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.460
Dropped out

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.820
Ridley honed her skills at England's Tring
Park School for the Performing Arts and graduated

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.850
with a concentration in musical theater in
2010.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.760
After that, she enrolled in London's Birkbeck
University where she studied classical civilization

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.210
— but kept going to auditions all the same.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.960
Before long she decided that if she wanted
to take acting seriously, she'd give it all

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.630
of her attention, and dropped out of school
to pursue it as a career.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:51.070
One of her very first jobs was on an interactive
first aid film in which she demonstrates how

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.809
to administer lifesaving CPR in a high-pressure
situation.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:57.040
She told Reconstruction Council UK,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.680
"This role was particularly important to me
as my godfather had suffered a cardiac arrest

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.830
some time before, and his life was saved because
there was someone with the knowledge to use

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.750
the right CPR techniques on him."

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.229
Smaller projects

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:14.820
Believe it or not, The Force Awakens was only
Ridley's second feature film, the first being

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.880
a 2012 movie called Scrawl created by filmmaker
Peter Hearn.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.650
Ridley popped onto Hearn's radar through a
connection from the set of a 2012 commercial

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.380
for British supermarket chain Morrisons.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.300
Ridley regularly worked on film projects by
Andover College students, and all she got

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.750
in return for her efforts was a refund on
the cost of her expenses.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.170
Hearn recalled being impressed by her strong
work ethic, telling The Guardian,

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.189
"I think she just wanted to work.

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:41.070
I'm pretty sure she was working in a bar at
the time we cast her.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:44.140
She was overwhelmed with the fact people were
offering her work.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.270
Whenever she got cast in anything we all applauded."

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.439
In an effort to bulk up her reel, Ridley accepted
the lead role in a short film called Blue

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:56.340
Season by filmmaker Georgia Higgins, created
as part of the 2013 Sci-Fi London 48-hour

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.340
challenge.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.340
Higgins told The Guardian,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.750
"She was focused and giving and open, asking
if there was anything she should change or

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:03.750
do.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.490
We didn't have much time for rehearsals and
she worked really well with that.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.400
For the first part of the film, she was mostly
hanging upside down."

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:11.460
"Really?"

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.060
"Yeah."

00:02:13.529 --> 00:02:14.520
Moving up

00:02:14.529 --> 00:02:19.279
Her hard work was soon rewarded with guest
parts in the British medical drama Casualty

00:02:19.279 --> 00:02:20.970
and the comedy drama Youngers.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:25.650
By 2014, Ridley had impressed TV producers
enough to start being considered for bigger

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:26.650
roles.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:30.560
She popped up as an enthusiastic shopper in
a season 2 episode of the popular drama Mr.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.879
Selfridge, and she also snagged a role in
a two-part Silent Witness special.

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:36.919
Unknown

00:02:36.919 --> 00:02:40.840
While all of this onscreen experience was
a good start for Ridley, she still thought

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.040
she was a million miles away from being able
to audition for a Hollywood blockbuster.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.700
Luckily for her, The Force Awakens director
J.J. Abrams wanted to cast unknown actors,

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.939
just as George Lucas did with the original
Star Wars trilogy.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:57.080
Abrams admitted to Elle that the casting process
was scary because of the inevitable scrutiny

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.250
ahead for these new actors.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.250
He added,

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.709
"So they needed to be actors whom the audience
could discover as these characters, not as

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:04.269
actors they'd seen elsewhere.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:08.559
Ideally, it needed to be people like Daisy
— somewhat experienced, but mostly new to

00:03:08.559 --> 00:03:10.139
the game."

00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:11.799
Nailed it

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:16.290
Abrams took a liking to Ridley right away,
but the audition process was still drawn out

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.290
and difficult.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.999
Ridley told The Telegraph in 2015,

00:03:18.999 --> 00:03:23.019
"I was just one of the lucky people who managed
to get an audition and he saw something in

00:03:23.019 --> 00:03:24.019
me.

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:27.250
I thought I'd ruined the first few auditions
but he saw some potential, I guess, and I

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.949
was allowed to come back and read again, and
then I finally got the role."

00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:35.279
Ridley secured the part with her fourth and
final reading, an emotionally charged audition

00:03:35.279 --> 00:03:36.900
that later found its way onto the internet.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.459
"I'm a crier.

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:49.019
I'm a big crier.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.580
I cried the other day."

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:53.680
Gym rat

00:03:53.689 --> 00:03:58.139
Ridley was understandably thrilled when she
got confirmation that she'd be playing Rey,

00:03:58.139 --> 00:04:01.269
but she knew that could change if she wasn't
physically prepared for the role.

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:05.769
According to Elle, to get into shape for Star
Wars, she ate a diet that consisted of "lots

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:10.720
of fish, legumes, and spirulina shakes" and
trained for at least four hours a day, four

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:11.720
days a week.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:16.060
In addition to intense indoor workouts that
included kickboxing and wall climbing, Ridley's

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.840
trainer had her performing sprints with a
parachute attached to her back in the parking

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.389
lot of Pinewood Studios.

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:26.300
While undeniably intense, that grueling workout
schedule is a small price to pay for a major

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.150
part in one of the most beloved film franchises
in Hollywood history.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.150
